webmvs: 'checkpoint' command + suspend/resume (sr.c) fixes. Applies after 0001-0014.

New commands
  checkpoint <dir> [level=0..9] [wait=ms] [screens=ms] [sync=0|1]
      Save the running machine without ending Hercules: stop the CPUs (<= 10 s), wait until no I/O is
      queued or active (wait=, default 10000 ms), then for every CCKD device under its CCKD I/O and file
      locks: flush the cache, wait for the writes, harden, copy each shadow file to <dir>/<name>; write
      <dir>/machine.srf (gzip level=, default 1; 0 = uncompressed), start the CPUs again, write
      <dir>/checkpoint.json last (deleted at the start). Any error: CPUs started again, HHC02031E.
      Success: HHC02030I with the pause time. screens= limits the 3270 Read Buffer per terminal
      (default 2000 ms; 0 = do not save the screens).
  srbuildid [id]   set (config or command) / show the build id written to every .srf

sr.c / console.c / cpu.c fixes
  - .srf header SR_HDR_BUILD (Hercules version + struct sizes + srbuildid id); resume refuses a file with
    another (HHC02023E) or no (HHC02024E) build id, before it changes anything
  - resume reads the whole file first (HHC02028E for a damaged/truncated file; machine unchanged)
  - started_mask written/read as 8 bytes (16-byte CPU_BITMAP: stock suspend failed, resume left the
    CPU stopped silently); sr_read_value rejects target sizes other than 1/2/4/8
  - SR_DEV_SENSE read into dev->sense (was dev->ecw)
  - CPU timer restored by resume is no longer overwritten by the stopped CPU's saved value (cpu.c)
  - resume clears the interrupt queue first and queues only the saved pending interrupts (was: every
    device's ioint/pciioint/attnioint queued, saved queue linked raw); the 3270 resume no longer dequeues
    the device's restored interrupts (terminals may connect before resume)
  - 3270 suspend Read Buffer: time limit, and terminal input that MVS has not read yet, or that arrives
    during the Read Buffer (also in the same recv() as the reply: record boundaries are tracked at each
    telnet EOR), is kept for MVS; the stock code lost it, and the terminal stayed locked (X SYSTEM)
  - console connection thread: does not read a terminal while an input record waits for MVS's read
    (recv_3270_data dropped that record when a Read Buffer reply woke the thread: lost keystroke)
  - an attention that device_attention rejects (device busy or interrupt pending) is raised again by
    the connection thread when the device is free (HHC02035I); the stock code dropped it
  - suspend restarts the CPUs when writing fails; resume closes the file; a resume that fails after it
    changed the machine configures the CPUs again (HHC02027W); HHC02026I on success

diff --git a/cckddasd.c b/cckddasd.c
index 29c9a34c..4ce7bc24 100644
--- a/cckddasd.c
+++ b/cckddasd.c
@@ -2028,6 +2028,191 @@ DEVBLK         *dev = data;             /* -> device block           */
